[{"current_page":17,"data":[{"id":238,"user_id":5,"type":"Tool","sub_type":"mutli-category","title":"OBELICS","publisher":"HuggingFace","authors":"HuggingFace","featuring":"Dataset","publish_date":"2023-06-30","link":"https:\/\/www.humata.ai\/","content":"<p>OBELICS is an open, large-scale, and filtered collection of 'interleaved image-text web documents, containing 141M English documents, 115B text tokens, and 353M images, extracted from Common Crawl dumps between February 2020 and February 2023'. HuggingFace published an accompanying <a href=\"https:\/\/huggingface.co\/papers\/2306.16527\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">paper<\/a> explicating their processes, as well as making the dataset available for public use and scrutiny, including the use of Spawning's API to integrate user training opt-outs. They include in terms of use a requirement for downstream developers to be transparent about their use of the dataset to train any model that is released.<\/p>","contact":null,"permission_status":null,"license":"CC-BY-4.0","example":null,"source":null,"editors":null,"image":null,"is_visible":1,"created_at":"2023-09-08T17:19:39.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-09-08T23:39:57.000000Z","pinned":0},{"id":237,"user_id":5,"type":"Resource","sub_type":"Essay","title":"AI and Music-Making Part 1: The State of Play","publisher":"Ableton","authors":"Angus Finlayson","featuring":null,"publish_date":"2023-05-30","link":"https:\/\/www.ableton.com\/en\/blog\/ai-and-music-making-the-state-of-play\/","content":null,"contact":null,"permission_status":null,"license":null,"example":null,"source":null,"editors":null,"image":null,"is_visible":1,"created_at":"2023-09-08T17:11:43.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-09-08T17:16:48.000000Z","pinned":0},{"id":235,"user_id":1,"type":"Tool","sub_type":"Audio","title":"Voicemod","publisher":null,"authors":"Voctro Labs","featuring":null,"publish_date":"2023-01-01","link":"https:\/\/control-api.voicemod.net\/","content":"<p>Real-time voice conversion technology<\/p>","contact":null,"permission_status":null,"license":null,"example":null,"source":null,"editors":null,"image":null,"is_visible":1,"created_at":"2023-09-06T17:12:32.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-09-06T17:13:33.000000Z","pinned":0},{"id":233,"user_id":1,"type":"Tool","sub_type":"Audio","title":"Tone Transfer \/ DDSP","publisher":null,"authors":"Magenta","featuring":null,"publish_date":"2020-12-01","link":"https:\/\/magenta.tensorflow.org\/ddsp-vst","content":"<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: #202124; background: #e9e9f0;\">DDSP morphs audio into a range of different instruments. Unlike MIDI notes, DDSP preserves the nuances of pitch and dynamics for expressive neural synthesis.<\/span> You can use Magenta&rsquo;s interface to try transfer between instruments or even build you own model.<\/p>","contact":null,"permission_status":null,"license":"Apache License 2.0","example":null,"source":null,"editors":null,"image":null,"is_visible":1,"created_at":"2023-09-06T16:38:57.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-09-06T16:46:16.000000Z","pinned":0},{"id":188,"user_id":1,"type":"Tool","sub_type":"Development","title":"Akash","publisher":null,"authors":"Akash","featuring":null,"publish_date":"2023-01-02","link":"https:\/\/akash.network\/","content":"<p>Akash is a peer-to-peer and open market to trade compute resources. Purpose-built for public utility, it is open source and aims to make compute sharable across start-ups and independent developers for training large ML models. They publish frequently and aim to make the resources needed for other ML tool development more accessible.<\/p>","contact":"AM","permission_status":null,"license":"Apache 2.0 Licensed. v0.22.8.","example":null,"source":null,"editors":null,"image":null,"is_visible":1,"created_at":"2023-01-27T08:57:36.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-09-08T23:43:00.000000Z","pinned":0}],"first_page_url":"https:\/\/creative-ai.org\